---
import "../styles.css"
---

<main class="landing troubleshooting-landing">
  <section class="hero troubleshooting-hero">
    <div class="hero__inner">
      <div class="hero__image">
        <img
          src="/canning-cover.png"
          alt="Canning Meat Cookbook for Beginners"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="hero__content">
        <p class="eyebrow">Free bonus guide</p>

        <h1>Fix Common Canning Meat Mistakes Before They Ruin Your Batch</h1>

        <p class="subtitle">
          Download your free <strong>Canning Meat Troubleshooting Guide</strong>
          and learn what to do when jars don’t seal, liquid disappears, meat
          changes color, or something simply looks wrong.
        </p>

        <ul class="benefits">
          <li>Identify the most common canning meat problems</li>
          <li>Know what’s normal, what’s risky, and what to discard</li>
          <li>Quick safety checks for seals, siphoning, fat, liquid loss, and discoloration</li>
        </ul>

        <button class="openModal button">
          Download the Free Troubleshooting Guide
        </button>

        <p class="privacy">
          No spam. Just practical canning help you’ll actually use.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="trust troubleshooting-trust">
    <h2>When something looks wrong, you need answers fast.</h2>
    <p>
      Canning meat can feel intimidating when a jar doesn’t behave as expected.
      This guide helps you understand the warning signs, avoid guesswork, and
      make safer decisions with confidence.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>What You’ll Find Inside</h2>

    <div class="pack-card">
      <div class="pack-item">
        <span>✓</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Common Error Explanations</h3>
          <p>
            Understand why jars fail to seal, why liquid loss happens, why fat
            may rise, and what changes in color or texture can mean.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pack-item">
        <span>✓</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Safe vs. Unsafe Clues</h3>
          <p>
            Learn which signs are usually harmless and which ones mean you
            should not take risks with the food inside the jar.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pack-item">
        <span>✓</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Quick Decision Checklist</h3>
          <p>
            Use a simple reference checklist when you need to decide whether to
            store, refrigerate, reprocess, or discard a jar.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="note">
      Designed to be kept near your canning station whenever a jar makes you pause.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="problem-section">
    <div class="problem-card">
      <h2>Because guessing is not a safety strategy</h2>

      <p>
        A failed seal, cloudy liquid, siphoning, or an unusual smell can leave
        you wondering what went wrong — and what to do next.
      </p>

      <ul class="simple-list">
        <li>Stop second-guessing every jar.</li>
        <li>Understand the most common pressure canning issues.</li>
        <li>Make calmer, safer decisions after processing.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        This guide gives you practical troubleshooting support so you can learn
        from mistakes without putting your pantry or your family at risk.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>How You’ll Use It</h2>

    <div class="steps">
      <div>
        <span>1</span>
        <h3>Spot the Problem</h3>
        <p>Check the jar, seal, liquid level, color, fat, smell, or texture.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <span>2</span>
        <h3>Find the Cause</h3>
        <p>Use the guide to understand what likely happened during processing.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <span>3</span>
        <h3>Take the Safe Next Step</h3>
        <p>Decide whether to store, refrigerate, reprocess, or discard.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="final-cta" id="signup">
    <h2>Troubleshoot Your Jars With Confidence</h2>

    <p>
      Download the free guide and keep a clear, practical safety reference close
      whenever you process canned meat.
    </p>

    <button class="openModal button" style="margin-top: 12px;">
      Download the Free Troubleshooting Guide
    </button>

    <p class="privacy">
      No spam. Just practical canning help you’ll actually use.
    </p>
  </section>
</main>

<div
  id="modal"
  class="fixed inset-0 hidden items-center justify-center bg-black bg-opacity-40 backdrop-blur-sm z-50"
>
  <div class="m-2 bg-white p-6 rounded-2xl shadow-2xl max-w-md w-full">
    <div class="flex justify-between items-start">
      <h2 style="padding-top: 40px">
        Get Your Free Troubleshooting Guide
      </h2>

      <button
        id="closeModal"
        class="text-gray-500 hover:text-black"
        aria-label="Close modal"
      >
        <svg
          xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
          class="w-5 h-5"
          fill="none"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          stroke="currentColor"
        >
          <path
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            stroke-width="2"
            d="M6 18L18 6M6 6l12 12"
          />
        </svg>
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="_form_3"></div>
    <script
      src="https://gahema.activehosted.com/f/embed.php?id=3"
      charset="utf-8"
    ></script>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  const modal = document.getElementById("modal");
  const openBtns = document.querySelectorAll(".openModal");
  const closeBtn = document.getElementById("closeModal");

  function openModal() {
    modal.classList.remove("hidden");
    modal.classList.add("flex");
  }

  function closeModal() {
    modal.classList.add("hidden");
    modal.classList.remove("flex");
  }

  openBtns.forEach((btn) => {
    btn.addEventListener("click", openModal);
  });

  closeBtn.addEventListener("click", closeModal);

  modal.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
    if (e.target === modal) closeModal();
  });

  document.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => {
    if (e.key === "Escape") closeModal();
  });
</script>